                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Shelter is essential. Until folks have a safe place to sleep, it\u2019s hard for them to start putting their lives back together.\n\nThat\u2019s exactly what Northview Pointe in Natomas is providing\u201466 furnished studio units for previously homeless individuals, along with on-site behavioral health support, case management, and community programming.\n\nThis project, led by Hope Cooperative and Excelerate Housing Group, shows what\u2019s possible when partners at the federal, state, and local levels come together to invest in affordable housing and mental health services.\n\nI know the next few years won\u2019t be easy for our nation and our community. We\u2019ll need to get creative, work together, support one another, and challenge old rules to deliver real solutions that lift up the most vulnerable among us.\n\nI\u2019ll continue working to lead that fight.",
                "text_lang": "en",
